<title>PERU: Peru's May mined iron output rises 11 percent.</title>
<headline>Peru's May mined iron output rises 11 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's iron output rose 11 percent to 253,527 tonnes in May compared with the same month last year, according to preliminary figures released Friday by the Energy and Mines Ministry.</p>
<p>Iron output fell 22 percent overall to 1.15 tonnes in the first five months against the same period last year, the ministry added in its monthly report.</p>
<p>Peru's only iron miner is Chinese-owned Shougang Hierro Peru S.A, a former state-owned firm privatized in November 1992.</p>
<p>((-- Andrew Cawthorne, Lima newsroom 511 221-2134))</p>
